// N10 checkpoint 2, R1 fix (PR #115 round 1): proves the literal JUMP_TABLE
// "out of [minTag, minTag+count) range" fallthrough is reachable.
//
// 26_enum_match_dispatch_and_error.lox's own header once claimed this path
// is NOT reachable from any program that compiles, reasoning that a
// table-eligible match is always exhaustive over its own enum's whole tag
// range. That reasoning covers only the ARMS: checkEnumExhaustiveness
// (compiler.cpp:1553-1568) checks that the arms name every constructor of
// THEIR OWN enum. It does not check the SUBJECT expression's own enum. Here
// the arms are exhaustive and dense over enum A (2 variants, tags 0 and 1),
// but the subject is R(), a value of the unrelated enum B (3 variants). B's
// own tag for R is 2 — outside A's [0, 2) range — so the emitted
// `tableswitch`'s own literal default label, not the sparse
// compare-and-branch form, is what raises MATCH_ERROR at run time.
//
// "before" proves the print above the match ran (so the match itself, not
// some earlier failure, is what raises the error); the emitted jasmin for
// this exact shape is in the PR body.
enum A { X Y }
enum B { P Q R }

print "before";
print match R() {
    case X => "x"
    case Y => "y"
};
